  "id": "schedule-induced-polydipsia",
  "term": "schedule-induced polydipsia",
  "definition": "Schedule-induced polydipsia is a laboratory task in which animals are assessed for excessive or compulsive drinking that develops under a scheduled procedure. In this packet, it is used to distinguish low- and high-compulsive drinking behavior in rats.",
